# Google OAuth Client ID for Drive sync (ERD §7.6).
# Create one in Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials:
#   1. Create a project (or pick an existing one).
#   2. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → "External", add yourself
#      as a test user, set app name "DayRail", support email = your own.
#   3. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Drive API".
#   4. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth Client
#      ID → Application type "Web application".
#   5. Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        http://localhost:5173        (dev)
#        http://localhost:4173        (vite preview)
#        https://<your-vercel-url>    (production)
#   6. (No redirect URI needed — GIS token client uses postMessage.)
#   7. Copy the resulting "Client ID" (a long .apps.googleusercontent.com
#      string) into the line below, save this file as `.env.local`.
#
# This file is checked into the repo as the template; .env.local is
# gitignored. Never commit a real client id.
VITE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
